---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — videomk">
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
		<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-neutral-500">Last updated: August 24, 2025</p>

		<p class="mt-6 text-neutral-700">
			This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, and disclose information about
			individuals who use our websites, applications, and related services (collectively, the
			“Services”). For the purposes of this Privacy Policy, “you” means the individual
			using the Services, whether as a visitor, customer, account holder, applicant, or other
			person interacting with us.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we
			will update the “Last updated” date above and, where required by law, provide additional
			notice (for example, on the Services or by email). If you do not agree to the updated
			policy, please discontinue use of the Services.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Information We Collect</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">We collect information about you from the following sources:</p>
		<div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-neutral-700">
			<section>
				<h3 class="font-medium text-neutral-900">Information You Provide</h3>
				<ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5">
					<li>Contact details (e.g., name, email, phone) for account and communication purposes.</li>
					<li>Account credentials and profile information to create and secure your account.</li>
					<li>Payment information processed by our payment provider for purchases.</li>
					<li>Applicant information (e.g., CV, job history) if you apply for a role.</li>
					<li>Prompts, questions, uploaded content, and generated outputs you create in the Services.</li>
					<li>Any other information you choose to include in communications with us.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h3 class="font-medium text-neutral-900">Information Collected Automatically</h3>
				<p class="mt-2">We and certain third parties collect Usage Data using cookies and similar technologies, including:</p>
				<ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5">
					<li>Device and browser information (e.g., type, OS, IP address).</li>
					<li>Approximate location (e.g., city, region).</li>
					<li>Interaction data (e.g., pages viewed, clicks, date/time, referring URLs).</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h3 class="font-medium text-neutral-900">Information From Other Sources</h3>
				<ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5">
					<li>Analytics providers to understand and improve how the Services are used.</li>
					<li>Business partners involved in offers or promotions.</li>
					<li>Authentication providers you choose to link (e.g., sign-in with a third party).</li>
					<li>Public sources, where allowed by law.</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-2">We may deidentify or aggregate information and use it for any lawful purpose.</p>
			</section>
		</div>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">How We Use Information</h2>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 text-neutral-700">
			<li>Provide, maintain, and improve the Services and related AI features.</li>
			<li>Operate, protect, and secure the Services; detect, prevent, and respond to fraud and abuse.</li>
			<li>Process transactions and fulfill requests.</li>
			<li>Communicate with you, including service and support messages.</li>
			<li>Conduct research, analytics, and product development.</li>
			<li>Comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			We use cookies and similar technologies to operate and measure the Services. Most browsers
			allow you to control cookies via settings. Blocking some cookies may impact functionality.
			Your browser may offer a Do Not Track signal; our Services are not configured to respond to
			these signals.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">How We Disclose Information</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">We disclose information as described below and as otherwise permitted by law:</p>
		<ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 text-neutral-700">
			<li>Service providers that support operations (e.g., hosting, security, payments, analytics).</li>
			<li>Business partners involved in promotions or providing access to the Services.</li>
			<li>Other parties at your direction, including when you share content publicly or via integrations.</li>
			<li>Professional advisors (e.g., auditors, legal counsel) and in connection with corporate transactions.</li>
			<li>Authorities or others when required by law, to protect rights and safety, or to enforce terms.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Social Features and Third‑Party Links</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			If you use features that interact with third‑party platforms, those platforms may collect and
			use information subject to their own policies. We are not responsible for third‑party practices.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Children’s Privacy</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			The Services are not intended for children under 13 (or the minimum age in your jurisdiction).
			We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If we learn that a child provided
			personal information, we will take reasonable steps to delete it.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Data Security and Retention</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			We use reasonable safeguards to protect information. No system is perfectly secure. We retain
			information as long as necessary for the purposes described above, including to provide the
			Services, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce agreements.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">International Data Transfers</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			Information may be processed in countries other than your own. Where required, we use
			appropriate safeguards for cross‑border transfers consistent with applicable law.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Your Rights and Choices</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			Depending on your location, you may have rights over your information, such as to request
			access, deletion, correction, portability, restriction or objection to processing, and to
			withdraw consent where processing is based on consent. We may take steps to verify your
			identity before responding. To exercise these rights, contact us using the details below.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">U.S. State Privacy Disclosures</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			If you are a resident of California or certain other U.S. states with similar privacy laws, you
			may have additional rights. In the last 12 months, we have collected the categories of personal
			information described in “Information We Collect.” We do not sell or share personal information
			as those terms are defined by applicable U.S. state laws. We will not discriminate against you for
			exercising your rights. You may designate an authorized agent to make certain requests on your
			behalf, subject to verification.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">How to Contact Us</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			Questions or requests? Email us at <a href="mailto:chris@chrisgenai.com" class="underline underline-offset-4">chris@chrisgenai.com</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-medium text-neutral-900">Language</h2>
		<p class="mt-2 text-neutral-700">
			If there is any inconsistency between versions of this policy in different languages, the
			English version will govern unless otherwise required by law.
		</p>

		<p class="mt-10">
			<a href="/" class="underline underline-offset-4">Back to home</a>
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
